# Lobby search over a fake Steam (H1): the host of the stand makes an invisible Steam lobby, the client
# waits for one, searches, finds the lobby, enters it by the id the search listed, and both play a few
# seconds: no member may report a desync.
#
# The stand's members meet over a fake Steam of the process, not the plain in-memory transport, and the
# lobby is `invisible` (a lobby search finds invisible and public lobbies, never friends-only or private
# ones). The first lobby of a fake Steam always has the id below. In process (cargo test --test steam)
# the stand is built by crates/shards_steam/tests/steam/scenarios.rs; against a live one:
#   cargo sandbox --features shards/steam --stand 1 --stand-steam --steam-lobby invisible --headless --paused --port 0 --port-file F &
#   SHARDS_PORT_FILE=F cargo shards wait              # the host: `wait --peer all` waits for the clients to join, and they wait for a lobby
#   SHARDS_PORT_FILE=F cargo shards scenario crates/shards_steam/scenarios/lobby_search.scenario
#   SHARDS_PORT_FILE=F cargo shards stand stop
stand clients=1
invariant !journal "desync"

# --- the stand: a lobby host (invisible), and a client that waits for a lobby
@host act steam
@host expect result contains "session: host · lobby 109775240917319681 (invisible: friends do not see it)"
@c1 act steam
@c1 expect result contains "waiting for an invite (or steam_join lobby=ID)"

# --- the client searches: the host's lobby is there, of its build, with room
@c1 act steam_lobbies
@c1 expect result contains "1 lobby of"
@c1 expect result contains "lobby 109775240917319681 · host"
@c1 expect result contains "build matches"
@c1 expect result contains "enter one with steam_join lobby=ID"
@c1 expect result !contains "note:"

# --- and enters it by that id
@c1 act steam_join lobby=109775240917319681
@c1 expect result contains "entered lobby 109775240917319681"
step 60
@c1 act steam
@c1 expect result contains "session: client · lobby 109775240917319681"
@host act steam
@host expect result contains "2 in it"
@host act steam_lobbies
@host expect result contains "· this game's lobby"

# --- both play a few seconds (the host's tick is the stand's): nobody left, nobody out of step
step 300
@host act net_status
@host expect result contains "\"desyncs\": 0"
@c1 act net_status
@c1 expect result contains "\"role\": \"client\""
@c1 expect result contains "\"desyncs\": 0"
